{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.BlockSDPNondegeneracy","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BlockSDPNondegeneracy","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.PosSemidefTraceZero"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BlockSDPNondegeneracy.feasible_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BlockSDPNondegeneracy.feasible_smul","kind":"theorem","line":174,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BlockSDPNondegeneracy.lean#L174-L185","doc":"**Homogeneity of degree one.**  Scaling a feasible point scales the target\nand the objective by the same factor.  This is precisely the property the LP\nlacks: there `n_target · y₀* = 0` for every target, so the optimal value is\nconstant in the target and prices nothing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BlockSDPNondegeneracy.exists_zero_obj_of_zero_weight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BlockSDPNondegeneracy.exists_zero_obj_of_zero_weight","kind":"theorem","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BlockSDPNondegeneracy.lean#L150-L170","doc":"**The O3 falsifier, formalised.**  A single block of vanishing weight is\nenough to produce a feasible point with objective `0` at *any* positive target,\nso the optimum collapses to `0` exactly as it does for the LP.  This is why O3\nhad to be amended to O3′: the hypothesis `∀ λ, 0 < y λ` above is doing real\nwork, and the `SU(2)` specialisation violates it for every `ℓ(λ) ≥ 3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BlockSDPNondegeneracy.obj_pos_of_pos_weights","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BlockSDPNondegeneracy.obj_pos_of_pos_weights","kind":"theorem","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BlockSDPNondegeneracy.lean#L135-L146","doc":"**O3′ is non-degenerate.**  If every surviving block carries a strictly\npositive weight, then every feasible point of the program has strictly positive\nobjective.  In particular the optimal value is not `0`, so — unlike the LP,\nwhose value is identically `0` for every target — the program prices its net\nconstraint. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BlockSDPNondegeneracy.exists_pos_of_net_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BlockSDPNondegeneracy.exists_pos_of_net_pos","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BlockSDPNondegeneracy.lean#L124-L133","doc":"A non-negative vector with strictly positive sum has a strictly positive\nentry. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BlockSDPNondegeneracy.trace_nonneg_of_posSemidef","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BlockSDPNondegeneracy.trace_nonneg_of_posSemidef","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BlockSDPNondegeneracy.lean#L114-L120","doc":"The trace of a positive-semidefinite real matrix is non-negative.  Supplies\nthe `0 ≤ t λ` hypothesis below from `Φ_λ ⪰ 0`, so nothing here is assumed of the\nblocks beyond feasibility. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BlockSDPNondegeneracy.net","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BlockSDPNondegeneracy.net","kind":"def","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BlockSDPNondegeneracy.lean#L108-L110","doc":"The net functional of the program: the total trace across blocks.  This is\nthe blockwise image of the LP's net constraint `Σ_i x_i = n_target`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BlockSDPNondegeneracy.obj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BlockSDPNondegeneracy.obj","kind":"def","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BlockSDPNondegeneracy.lean#L104-L106","doc":"The block-diagonal operator-selection objective: a weighted sum of block\ntraces.  `y λ` is the Markov/Plancherel weight of block `λ`, `t λ = tr Φ_λ`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}